  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration. Verify every task in TASK-INDEX is ✅ (or explicitly deferred with a note) — if not, STOP: this task's gate is unmet.</step>
    <step order="1">Invoke /test-diet; review the classification; save the report; do NOT execute deletions — hand the emitted commands to the reviewer via the PR.</step>
    <step order="2">H-8a: remove/replace the stale ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter/ExternalCallerContext comment references (grep-verified complete list); comment-only diff.</step>
    <step order="3">H-8b: check FR-16's (A-13) merged fix; then remove the vestigial WebRoleRemoved field + dead SPE-removal remainder per the consumer-grep constraint; document the disposition.</step>
    <step order="4">Write notes/lessons-learned.md: what the investigation-first approach caught (F1 refutation shaping FR-26), the reclassification of the BU restructure to UAT, the POA consolidation reuse story, evaluator-versioning decisions, and process lessons for the next access project.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify success criteria 1-9 in spec.md each have their verification pointer (test name / UAT item); record the mapping in the README status section.</step>
    <step order="6">Update README to Complete; reconcile TASK-INDEX; reset current-task.md to "none"; build green; publish size reported.</step>
    <step order="7">Wrap-up PR citing the test-diet report + register closeouts.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If H-8b's WebRoleRemoved field is read by ANY client, or the SPE-removal path turns out to be live behaviour post-FR-16, STOP the removal and record a path-A disposition (kept + deprecated, reason documented) instead — a wrap-up task must not ship a breaking contract change.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
